menu "Opus playback"

    config OPUS_PLAYER
        bool "Enable Ogg Opus playback"
        default n
        depends on MQJS_TAB5_AUDIO
        help
            Decode an in-memory Ogg Opus stream with the float Opus
            component and send signed 16-bit PCM to audio_tab5.

    config OPUS_PLAYER_BOOT_OPUS
        bool "Embed assets/audio/tab5-boot-48k.opus"
        default n
        depends on OPUS_PLAYER
        help
            Embed the 48 kbit/s stereo Opus fixture so it can be played
            without a filesystem.

    config OPUS_PLAYER_BOOT_AUTOPLAY
        bool "Play the embedded Opus fixture at boot"
        default n
        depends on OPUS_PLAYER_BOOT_OPUS
        depends on !MQJS_TAB5_AUDIO_SELFTEST
        help
            Start asynchronous playback from the UI/I2C ready event.
            Intended for initial device verification.
            The speaker self-test option must be off so only one producer
            owns the PCM stream.

    config OPUS_PLAYER_DIAGNOSTICS
        bool "Log decoded PCM diagnostics"
        default n
        depends on OPUS_PLAYER
        help
            Log the first decoded samples, min/max, and an FNV-1a hash of
            the first 4096 output frames. Intended for decoder validation.

endmenu
